From 7514cf23e1e4bb0052a871b1143e6b36afd5e207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:01:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Try-on server: close the abuse and privacy gaps from
 the security review

The IP limit now keys on the platform's hop (the last public X-Forwarded-For
entry), not the caller's own first entry. A photo the checks refuse gives the
device its try back but keeps the address row spent, so one address can no
longer burn the day's cap. tryon_refund locks its rows in tryon_take's order
(pgbench had found deadlocks), the sweeps run at the start of every take, and
the ledger write and refunds are bounded so they never hold a reply past the
deadline. A pre-check stopped by the model's safety filter is refused before
the paid render, /feedback writes nothing while switched off and keeps the
first report only, the 429 carries the device allowance, and the privacy
notice now names the 90-day ledger, the order attribute and the salt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpEhS3XnffjKP5JTdNrd3V
