+- Abuse limits (security review, 30 Oct): the IP limit is keyed on the LAST
+  public X-Forwarded-For entry (the platform's hop), never the first (the
+  caller writes that one). A photo the checks refuse gives the device its try
+  back but leaves the address row spent, so one address can spend at most
+  `TRYON_IP_DAILY` of the day's global cap. The preview smoke confirms the
+  hop: send `X-Forwarded-For: 192.0.2.1` and read the log line; `ipTestNet:
+  true` means the platform passes a client's header through unchanged and the
+  key must move (to `cf-connecting-ip`, if Supabase forwards it). Quota keys
+  and 90-day ledger rows are swept at the start of every `tryon_take`; if the
+  try-on is switched off for more than a day, run `delete from
+  public.tryon_quota` so the privacy notice's two days still hold.
 - Nothing goes to Meta: no new pixel or CAPI event. AddToCart still fires only
   from CartContext. Clarity gets allow-listed event names only
